From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winegstreamer: color converter IMediaObject, IPropertyStore, MFT status and messages; drop IPropertyBag

Same work as the resampler patch, on the color converter, using the helpers
of dmo_transform.c:

- IMediaObject: stream count / info, GetInputType (the 20 input subtypes,
  without format block), GetOutputType (the 16 output subtypes; once an input
  type is set they carry its frame size, rate, stride and image size in a
  VIDEOINFOHEADER), Set/Get types (VIDEOINFOHEADER and VIDEOINFOHEADER2),
  size info (one frame), latency, Lock, streaming resources, input status,
  Discontinuity, Flush, ProcessInput / ProcessOutput with IMediaBuffer
  (time stamp and length carried to the output, S_FALSE without output).
- IMFTransform GetInputStatus, DRAIN / FLUSH / notification messages,
  ProcessEvent and GetOutputStatus (documented E_NOTIMPL, no FIXME).
- IPropertyStore keeps its values.
- The conformance test expects IPropertyBag to be absent from the color
  converter (check_interface(..., FALSE), marked todo): the object no longer
  offers it, with its Read / Write stubs, and the todo_wine is removed.

